{
 "_about": "The patch queue, its journal and undo, one way for the Python Editor and the viewer's: run by tests/test_queue_cases.py (PatchQueue, editor.queue_journal, restore_queue, the session's undo history) and viewer-shell/editcore/tests/cases.rs (editcore::queue). Each case is a list of operations on an empty queue: [\"whole\", type, key, plugin], [\"field\", type, key, path, {\"plugin\": p} | {\"value\": v}], [\"base\", type, key, plugin], [\"remove_record\", type, key], [\"remove_field\", type, key, path], [\"ref\", cell, origin, index, changes, plugins], [\"remove_ref\", cell, origin, index, path or null], [\"made\", type, key, record, source, topic], [\"remove_made\", type, key], [\"new\", cell, uid, fields, base, plugins, tag], [\"remove_new\", cell, uid], [\"snapshot\", name], [\"restore\", name], [\"consume\", name], [\"clear\"], [\"restore_journal\", document], [\"step\"] (a change ends: the undo history records it), [\"undo\"], [\"redo\"]. `expect`: the journal's document after them, the queue's length (records the patch carries), its revision (changes counted), what each restore brought back, whether each undo or redo had a step, and the undo and redo steps left. Rules: re-deciding replaces; whole or merged, never both; a journal's decisions come back unless the queue holds them; a build consumes only what it wrote. Generated from the Python side when a case is added, and read by hand.",
